-- Wikimedia Commons and loc.gov were unreachable from the newsroom sandbox on this run. Photo URLs are Commons thumbnail URLs built from file names found in web search (MD5 path); licenses were read from Commons file-page mirrors. Editor: confirm each photo loads and matches its caption; the image check removes any that do not.
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO stories (id, slug, lane, type, section_slug, status, sensitive, headline, dek, body, byline, hero_image_url, hero_image_credit, hero_image_rights, source_system, source_ref, priority, is_lead_candidate, created_by, created_at, updated_at) VALUES ('bd-20261109-hegseth-impeachment', 'congress-returns-massie-hegseth-impeachment-vote-leadership-elections-lame-duck', 'newsroom', 'news_story', 'congress', 'EDITORIAL_REVIEW', 0, 'Congress returns on Monday, Nov. 9, as Thomas Massie moves to force a House vote on impeaching Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth', 'The Kentucky Republican could act as early as Monday, Nov. 9, setting up a vote midweek. House and Senate Republicans also pick leaders on Tuesday, Nov. 10, and government funding runs out after Friday, Dec. 11.', 'Congress comes back on Monday, Nov. 9, for a five-week lame-duck session, and its first big fight may be over Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth.

Rep. Thomas Massie, a Kentucky Republican who lost his primary earlier this year, is expected to reintroduce a privileged resolution to impeach Hegseth. A privileged resolution lets a single member force the House to take it up. Massie''s measure carries eight articles, and he could file it as early as Monday, Nov. 9, which would set up a vote in the middle of the week, ABC News reported.

## Republican support is wavering

Multiple Republican sources told CNN they expected the measure to pass the House, according to a CNN Newsource report carried by KBTX. Many Republicans blame Hegseth for persuading President Trump to attack Iran without an exit strategy, and Vice President JD Vance is among those who have linked the Iran war to the party''s midterm losses, ABC News reported.

Hegseth answered in a video on X, calling the articles a "sham" pushed by a "disgruntled, defeated congressman" and his Democratic allies, Newsweek reported. Massie has said he would not file the resolution if Hegseth resigned.

Trump has said he will keep Hegseth. In his *60 Minutes* interview, which aired on Sunday, Nov. 8, he said he has confidence in the defense secretary, according to the CBS News transcript. Even if the House impeaches Hegseth, removing him would take a two-thirds vote in the Senate.

## Leadership votes on Tuesday

- **House Republicans** vote on Tuesday, Nov. 10, on who will lead them in the minority. Majority Leader Steve Scalise and Judiciary Committee Chairman Jim Jordan are running, after Speaker Mike Johnson said he would not seek the post.
- **Senate Republicans** hold a closed-door leadership vote on the morning of Tuesday, Nov. 10. All current leaders are seeking to keep their jobs, and no major changes are expected.
- **House Democrats** pick their leaders on Wednesday, Nov. 18, and are expected to nominate Hakeem Jeffries for speaker.
- **Senate Democrats** have not set a date. Chuck Schumer is building support to become majority leader.

## The rest of the list

Government funding runs out after Friday, Dec. 11, and lawmakers are far from a deal to avoid a shutdown, ABC News reported. Congress also has to pass the annual defense policy bill, renew the Section 702 surveillance authority and deal with the expired farm bill. Senate Republicans want to confirm Trump''s remaining nominees before they lose the majority.

The Senate holds a procedural vote on Monday, Nov. 9, on a bipartisan permitting package. In the House, Massie''s discharge petition on a second Epstein files bill has 216 of the 218 signatures it needs to force a floor vote.

The new Congress is sworn in on Sunday, Jan. 3. It will include at least 109 House freshmen, the largest class elected before a Congress convenes since 1933, according to ABC News.', 'Boston Daily Staff', 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/US_Navy_051128-N-2383B-013_An_aerial_view_of_the_headquarters_of_the_United_States_Department_of_Defense_located_between_the_Potomac_River_and_Arlington_National_Cemetery.jpg/1280px-US_Navy_051128-N-2383B-013_An_aerial_view_of_the_headquarters_of_the_United_States_Department_of_Defense_located_between_the_Potomac_River_and_Arlington_National_Cemetery.jpg', 'An aerial view of the Pentagon, between the Potomac River and Arlington National Cemetery, 2005 (file). Photo: U.S. Navy via Wikimedia Commons, public domain', 'public_domain', 'newsroom', 'content/2026-11-09.sql', 9, 1, 'newsroom-assistant', '2026-11-09T10:50:00.000Z', '2026-11-09T10:50:00.000Z');
